---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';

const url = 'https://barmooncontracting.com/services/general-contracting-harker-heights-tx';

const pageSchemas = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'Service',
    serviceType: 'General Contracting',
    name: 'General Contracting in Harker Heights, TX',
    description:
      'General contractor for Harker Heights homes—repairs, renovations, outdoor living, fencing, roofing, and multi-trade project management in Bell County.',
    provider: { '@type': 'GeneralContractor', name: 'Bar Moon Contracting', url: 'https://barmooncontracting.com/' },
    areaServed: [
      { '@type': 'City', name: 'Harker Heights, TX' },
      { '@type': 'AdministrativeArea', name: 'Bell County, TX' },
    ],
    url,
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://barmooncontracting.com/' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Services', item: 'https://barmooncontracting.com/services' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: 'General Contracting in Harker Heights, TX', item: url },
    ],
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'FAQPage',
    mainEntity: [
      {
        '@type': 'Question',
        name: 'Do you work throughout Harker Heights?',
        acceptedAnswer: {
          '@type': 'Answer',
          text: 'Yes. We serve established and newer neighborhoods across Harker Heights, plus nearby Nolanville and Killeen corridors when the project fits our service radius.',
        },
      },
      {
        '@type': 'Question',
        name: 'Can one contractor handle a remodel and outdoor work together?',
        acceptedAnswer: {
          '@type': 'Answer',
          text: 'Yes. Many Harker Heights projects combine interior updates with fencing, patios, or drainage. We sequence trades so exterior and interior work do not fight each other on the calendar.',
        },
      },
      {
        '@type': 'Question',
        name: 'Do you pull permits in Harker Heights?',
        acceptedAnswer: {
          '@type': 'Answer',
          text: 'Yes. We handle permitting and inspections for work that requires them, and we explain what does and does not need a permit before you sign.',
        },
      },
      {
        '@type': 'Question',
        name: 'How quickly can you start a smaller repair job?',
        acceptedAnswer: {
          '@type': 'Answer',
          text: 'Smaller repairs often schedule within days to a couple of weeks depending on material and crew load. Larger remodels are scheduled after a written proposal is approved.',
        },
      },
    ],
  },
];
---

<Layout
  title="General Contracting in Harker Heights, TX | Bar Moon Contracting"
  description="Harker Heights general contractor for renovations, repairs, outdoor living, fencing, and roofing—clear planning and one point of contact for Bell County homes."
  schemas={pageSchemas}
>
  <Header />

  <main class="pt-20 bg-light-neutral text-primary">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 py-20">
      <div class="mb-8 text-sm text-gray-600">
        <a href="/services" class="text-accent hover:underline">Services</a>
        <span class="mx-2">/</span>
        <span>General Contracting in Harker Heights, TX</span>
      </div>

      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold mb-6">General Contracting in Harker Heights, TX</h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-700 mb-10">
        Harker Heights homeowners often need more than a single trade—they need someone who can line up a kitchen
        update, a fence that will not fail in the first storm season, and exterior work that matches the
        neighborhood. Bar Moon Contracting runs those projects as one plan, one schedule, and one phone number.
      </p>

      <div class="prose max-w-none text-gray-700 mb-16 space-y-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl">Built for Harker Heights neighborhoods</h2>
        <p>
          Harker Heights grew as a residential bridge between Killeen and Nolanville, with established streets,
          HOA-style subdivisions, and a steady pace of remodels driven by families who want better kitchens,
          outdoor living, and curb appeal without starting over. Projects here frequently stack: replace a
          failing fence while the patio is open, fix drainage that has been soaking a slab edge, or refresh paint
          and roofing in the same season so the exterior ages evenly.
        </p>
        <p>
          That is where general contracting earns its keep. Hiring four separate vendors means four schedules,
          four excuses, and no one owning the handoff between trades. We own the sequence—what happens first,
          what can overlap, and what has to wait on inspection—so you are not managing a jobsite from a group
          text.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl">Services we provide in Harker Heights</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Repairs, maintenance, and multi-room renovations</li>
          <li>Kitchen and bath updates as part of a larger remodel package</li>
          <li>Painting, roofing, and exterior finish work</li>
          <li>Outdoor living: decks, patios, covers, and hardscape coordination</li>
          <li>Fencing and concrete work suited to heat and soil movement</li>
          <li>Storm repairs and insurance-claim documentation support</li>
          <li>Trade coordination (electrical, plumbing, HVAC) under one GC lead</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl">Site and climate notes for this side of Bell County</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Heat and UV.</strong> West Bell County sun is hard on fences, deck boards, and exterior paint.
          We specify materials and prep that match exposure—not the cheapest board that looks fine for one
          season.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Storms and wind.</strong> Sudden storms can lift shingles, drive water into weak flashings, and
          overwhelm gutters that were never sized for the roof. Exterior scopes include how water leaves the
          property, not just how the finish looks on day one.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Clay and grading.</strong> Like much of the region, expansive soils and poor grading create
          recurring cracks and door-swing issues. When we open a patio, fence line, or addition, we look at how
          the ground is already behaving so the new work does not fight the old.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Neighbor density.</strong> Many Harker Heights lots sit close to neighboring homes. We keep
          jobsite noise and debris reasonable, protect shared edges, and communicate when deliveries or noisy
          work will happen—small details that matter in established subdivisions.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl">How we run projects here</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>
            <strong>Listen first</strong> — Goals, budget range, and any HOA or neighbor constraints you already
            know about.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Scope on paper</strong> — What is included, what is excluded, and which allowances you still
            need to choose.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Sequence the work</strong> — Interior and exterior phases ordered so crews are not tripping
            over each other.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Build and communicate</strong> — Daily or phase-based updates; written change orders if the
            plan shifts.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Close clean</strong> — Walkthrough, punch list, and a site left ready for normal life again.
          </li>
        </ol>

        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl">Harker Heights FAQs</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Do you work throughout Harker Heights?</strong> Yes. We serve established and newer
          neighborhoods across Harker Heights, plus nearby Nolanville and Killeen corridors when the project fits
          our service radius.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Can one contractor handle a remodel and outdoor work together?</strong> Yes. Many Harker Heights
          projects combine interior updates with fencing, patios, or drainage. We sequence trades so exterior and
          interior work do not fight each other on the calendar.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Do you pull permits in Harker Heights?</strong> Yes. We handle permitting and inspections for
          work that requires them, and we explain what does and does not need a permit before you sign.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>How quickly can you start a smaller repair job?</strong> Smaller repairs often schedule within
          days to a couple of weeks depending on material and crew load. Larger remodels are scheduled after a
          written proposal is approved.
        </p>

        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
          Nearby service pages:{' '}
          <a href="/services/kitchen-bath-remodeling-killeen-tx" class="text-accent hover:underline"
            >Kitchen &amp; bath in Killeen</a
          >
          {' · '}
          <a href="/services/general-contracting-belton-tx" class="text-accent hover:underline"
            >General contracting in Belton</a
          >
          {' · '}
          <a href="/services/outdoor-living-decks-patios-central-texas" class="text-accent hover:underline"
            >Outdoor living</a
          >
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-deep-blue text-white p-8 rounded-2xl">
        <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Need a general contractor in Harker Heights?</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-white/90">One plan for interior and exterior work—clear pricing, local conditions, no chaos.</p>
        <a href="/get-quote" class="inline-block bg-accent hover:bg-gold text-dark-blue font-bold px-8 py-3 rounded-lg"
          >Get a Free Quote</a
        >
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm">
          Call or text: <a href="tel:2545813808" class="text-gold-primary">(254) 581-3808</a> · Mon–Fri 8:00 AM –
          6:00 PM
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
